# SvelteKit Standards

## Style

- 2-space indent; TypeScript throughout
- Domain types in `src/lib/types.ts`; API client in `src/lib/api.ts`
- Components in `src/lib/components/`; routes under `src/routes/`

## Patterns

- **Data loading:** `+page.ts` load functions for server-side fetch where appropriate; keep components presentational
- **Auth:** store JWT client-side (sessionStorage or cookie per your choice); redirect to `/login` on `401`
- **API calls:** use `PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` from env — never hardcode API host
- **No secrets in frontend:** only `PUBLIC_*` env vars in browser code

## UI scope

- Login page + dashboard (metrics cards, expiring table, date range filter)
- Reuse components: `MetricsCard`, `DateRangeFilter`, `RecordsTable`, `StatusBadge`
- Status badges must reflect enum values: `active`, `expiring`, `expired`, `renewed`, `archived`

## API alignment

- Match response shapes in `docs/api-doc.md` (`/dashboard/metrics`, `/dashboard/expiring`)
- Send `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on all requests except login
- Handle paginated envelopes: `{ data, total, limit, offset }`

## Tests

- Colocate `*.test.ts` under `src/lib/` (Vitest when configured)

## Accessibility & UX

- Show loading and error states for API calls
- Date displays: user-friendly format; API uses `YYYY-MM-DD`
